    <sys:String x:Key="Battery.EmergencyReserveNote">This estimated reserve is the energy between the normal utility-transfer level and the protected minimum. The protected minimum is the lower level the system tries not to cross to protect the battery, especially during outages or exceptional operation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Battery.ThresholdSourceCurrent">Observed current thresholds: grid {0:N0}% · protected floor {1:N0}% · return {2:N0}%. They match the expected family policy.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Battery.ThresholdSourceCurrentDrift">Observed current thresholds: grid {0:N0}% · protected floor {1:N0}% · return {2:N0}%. They differ from the family policy; the app is showing the inverter's current values.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Battery.ThresholdSourceManual">Not all current thresholds have a validated reading. Family policy is used as fallback: grid {0:N0}% · protected floor {1:N0}% · return {2:N0}%.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.BatteryRemaining">An estimate of the energy left in the battery. It is calculated from charge percentage and configured usable capacity; it is not a separate measurement.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tooltip.BatteryActivity">Shows whether the battery is receiving energy, supplying energy, or nearly at rest based on inverter readings.</sys:String>

